openmediavault-filebrowser-quantum (8.1.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fail-closed start and storage identity:
    - The shared folder identity is a UUID again. 'My Photos' and
      'My_Photos' both derived '/srv/My_Photos' and the storage source
      form resolved that value to the first matching folder, so a source
      could mount a folder the operator did not select. Colliding names
      now get a deterministic UUID suffix and an ambiguous value is
      rejected instead of being mapped.
    - start/restart/upgrade run the same preconditions as the ctl
      (enabled, data folder present, at least one resolvable source, no
      pending Apply); 'omv-filebrowserquantum-ctl up' is fail-closed
      itself, so a direct call cannot bypass them either.
    - A stack that is still registered while the configuration became
      incomplete (data folder or the last storage source removed) is
      unregistered instead of being left behind with the old bind mounts.
      The mask check now verifies the bind set in both directions.
  * Upstream configuration and data protection:
    - Authentication, base URL and external URL are written to
      config.yaml (auth.methods.*, http.baseURL, http.externalUrl). The
      unsupported FILEBROWSER_NOAUTH / FILEBROWSER_BASEURL /
      APPLICATION_URL environment variables are gone; a proxy
      authentication header can be configured.
    - config.yaml is parsed strictly (an unparsable file aborts the start
      instead of being overwritten), merged with the operator's own keys
      and written atomically with a backup copy.
    - Clearing the base URL really clears it, and the external URL is
      written as origin only, so the Open button cannot produce
      /files/files any more.
    - Disabling the automatic masking no longer exposes the Compose
      configuration tree: storage sources that contain a protected root
      are rejected instead.
  * Upgrade and feedback:
    - Upgrade resolves the latest upstream release, advances a pinned
      image tag in the configuration, re-renders the stack and only then
      pulls the image and recreates the container; a failing pull aborts
      the task instead of being ignored.
    - The Salt state fails when the container is not running or Docker
      reports it unhealthy, and the health state is shown in the UI.
    - Buttons follow the real state (configured/enabled/running), a
      "Refresh status" button reloads status, running version and mask
      preview, and a failing "Check for latest version" shows the reason
      instead of a success notification.
    - Advisory PUID/PGID permission check with root and ACL hints, so a
      permission problem is visible before the container answers 403.
  * Tests and documentation:
    - The Python suite imports the shipped fbq_tools.py, so the anti
      recursion, gate and config.yaml code is executed instead of a copy
      of it; the R-7 limit test is real. New PHP cases cover the
      collision mapping, the URL round trip, the upgrade tag decision and
      the stack revocation.
    - validate-workbench.py validates the constraint structure (the
      malformed requiredIf was not caught before) and rejects a ': '
      inside a msgid.
    - README rewritten for the multi source architecture; the unused
      RESTRICTED_VOLUME_PREFIX is removed and the nested datamodel path
      default is empty, consistent with the standalone model.

