openmediavault-filebrowser-quantum (8.1.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Let the container path follow the selected shared folder again:
    - The hidden autoPath baseline was declared before the container path
      field, so it was updated before the modifier that compares against
      it ran. Switching the shared folder therefore never re-derived the
      path once a folder had been picked. The field order is swapped so
      the comparison sees the previous baseline and an untouched path
      follows the new folder; customized paths are still preserved.
    - The container path hint no longer claims that clearing the field
      fills it in immediately (an empty path is generated when saving).
  * Remove the hard rejection of the production restricted volume:
    - Red line #9 only restricts the AI agent from reading that volume,
      it does not forbid the operator from mounting it. Blocking it in
      assertNotRestrictedVolume() made 'volume1' unselectable as a
      storage source (500 "points to a restricted volume"). Operators may
      now expose it like any other shared folder; the R-1..R-7 recursion
      and credential masking rules are unchanged.

